---
const stages = [
  ['Find the PunchOut catalog', 'A JAGGAER buyer selects the supplier PunchOut source from the procurement shopping experience.'],
  ['Shop in Shopify', 'PunchOut Central opens the supplier’s configured Shopify catalog, with buyer-specific access.'],
  ['Return the cart', 'The selected products return to the JAGGAER purchasing flow for requisition review and approval.'],
  ['Receive the PO', 'Confirm the buyer’s chosen order-delivery method. An approved PO received by PunchOut Central creates the Shopify order.'],
  ['Handle the invoice', 'PunchOut Central records invoice activity; the buyer’s invoice submission method is configured separately.']
];
---
<main>
  <section class="page-hero page-hero--mint" id="overview"><div class="wrap page-hero__grid">
    <div class="page-hero__copy reveal"><span class="ey">Shopify JAGGAER PunchOut</span><h1>Bring your Shopify catalog into JAGGAER buying.</h1><p class="lead">JAGGAER supports supplier PunchOut catalogs in its purchasing flow. PunchOut Central connects the buyer’s cXML catalog session to your Shopify storefront and keeps the later PO and order linked.</p><div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Discuss a JAGGAER buyer &rarr;</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="#details">Review onboarding &darr;</a></div></div>
    <div class="hero-visual logo-hero reveal"><div class="hero-visual__label"><span>Buyer system</span><b>Supplier PunchOut</b></div><div class="logo-hero__mark"><strong>JAGGAER</strong></div><span class="logo-hero__status">PunchOut Central</span><h3>JAGGAER to Shopify</h3><p>Buyer-side catalog and approval; supplier-side shopping and order.</p></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec" id="flow"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head center reveal"><span class="ey">JAGGAER workflow</span><h2>From PunchOut selection to approved PO.</h2><p class="lead">JAGGAER’s eProcurement flow moves from catalog shopping through cart, requisition and purchase order. Shopify remains the supplier catalog, not the buyer’s purchasing system.</p></div>
    <div class="integration-flow reveal"><div class="integration-node"><strong>JAGGAER</strong><span>Buyer cart and requisition</span></div><div class="integration-arrow">&rarr;</div><div class="integration-node integration-node--accent"><strong>PunchOut Central</strong><span>Connection and transaction</span></div><div class="integration-arrow">&rarr;</div><div class="integration-node"><strong>Shopify</strong><span>Supplier storefront</span></div></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec soft" id="details"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Supplier enablement</span><h2>Confirm the catalog and document channels separately.</h2><p class="lead">JAGGAER’s supplier enablement terms describe cXML PunchOut. They also list multiple order-delivery and invoicing options, so a PunchOut session does not by itself establish the PO or invoice channel.</p></div>
    <div class="simple-steps">{stages.map(([title, description], index) => <article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{description}</p></article>)}</div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec" id="proof"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Buyer testing</span><h2>Test the full JAGGAER handoff.</h2><p class="lead">Verify that the buyer can access the PunchOut catalog, returned items appear in the requisition, the approved PO reaches the agreed channel, and the resulting Shopify order matches it. Test invoice delivery only against the method the buyer selected.</p></div>
    <div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card reveal" href="/integrations/cxml/"><span>Protocol</span><h3>cXML</h3><p>Review the catalog-session protocol.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a><a class="related-card reveal" href="/platform/purchase-orders/"><span>Order stage</span><h3>Purchase orders</h3><p>See the PO-to-store-order handoff.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a><a class="related-card reveal" href="/platform/invoices/"><span>After ordering</span><h3>Invoices</h3><p>See invoice activity in the transaction.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a></div>
    <p><small>Buyer-side references: <a href="https://www.jaggaer.com/wp-content/uploads/JAGGAER-eProcurement-Product-Brief.pdf">JAGGAER eProcurement product brief</a> and <a href="https://www.jaggaer.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/JAGGAER-Supplier-Enablement-terms.pdf">supplier enablement terms</a>.</small></p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec soft" id="faq"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head center reveal"><span class="ey">FAQ</span><h2>JAGGAER questions</h2></div><div class="faq reveal">
    <div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>What protocol is used for JAGGAER PunchOut?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>JAGGAER’s supplier enablement documentation specifies cXML for PunchOut catalog enablement. Confirm the buyer’s exact settings during onboarding.</p></div></div>
    <div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Does JAGGAER always send POs by cXML?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>No. JAGGAER lists several order-delivery methods. The buyer and supplier must agree on the method for this connection.</p></div></div>
    <div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Is invoice submission part of cart return?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>No. The cart returns for purchasing approval. Invoice activity is later and the buyer’s submission method is a separate setup decision.</p></div></div>
  </div></div></section>
  <section class="page-cta"><div class="wrap reveal"><span class="ey">Set up the buyer flow</span><h2>Review JAGGAER catalog, PO and invoice requirements.</h2><p class="lead">Bring the buyer’s supplier-enablement details and your Shopify catalog structure.</p><div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Book a demo &rarr;</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="/integrations/shopify/">Explore Shopify PunchOut</a></div></div></section>
</main>
